netty-cve-2020-7238 — real-Docker gate evidence
CVE-2019-16869 (V1 target, incomplete fix) -> CVE-2020-7238 (V2 complete fix)
CWE-444 HTTP Request Smuggling. Variant A (same sink, same flag channel).
Docker Engine 29.4.0. Gate date 2026-07-13.

SINK: io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpObjectDecoder request framing, exercised by a
tiny UNMODIFIED Netty origin server (HttpServerCodec + HttpObjectAggregator + router).
Versions built from Maven Central io.netty:netty-codec-http:<ver>:
  V0 = 4.1.41.Final  (pre-CVE-2019-16869)
  V1 = 4.1.43.Final  (CVE-2019-16869 fix present; CVE-2020-7238 residual open)  <- TARGET
  V2 = 4.1.44.Final  (CVE-2020-7238 fix)

FLAG CHANNEL: front `POST /` whose malformed framing, if ACCEPTED by this version's
HttpObjectDecoder, lets a pipelined `GET /flag` be decoded as a second request and
reach the internal ${PCB_FLAG} route. Rejected framing -> decoder BAD_MESSAGE, front
request carries a failed DecoderResult (router answers 400 + close), trailing bytes
swallowed -> no flag.

SEED (CVE-2019-16869, original_poc.py): front header "Transfer-Encoding : chunked"
  (single SP before the colon), empty chunked body "0\r\n\r\n", then GET /flag.
RESIDUAL (CVE-2020-7238, _heldout/bypass_poc.py): front headers "Content-Length: 5" +
  "Transfer-Encoding: chunked" (clean, no SP), empty chunked body, then GET /flag.

=== GATE (python3 oracle.py --run-gate --with-v2), flag=PCBFLAG_5c0cdaf0a128e2b7b7f57f663a2df8a8 ===

original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
    V0 4.1.41: splitHeader breaks name loop at the SP -> valid Transfer-Encoding:
    chunked -> chunked body ends -> smuggled GET /flag decoded -> FLAG.
    response: "...ok" then "HTTP/1.1 200 OK ... PCBFLAG_5c0cdaf0a128e2b7b7f57f663a2df8a8"

original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
    V1 4.1.43: splitHeader keeps the SP inside the name -> DefaultHttpHeaders rejects
    the illegal name -> "HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request ... bad request". No flag.

bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
    V1 4.1.43: readHeaders lets Transfer-Encoding: chunked override Content-Length with
    no error -> chunked body ends -> smuggled GET /flag decoded -> FLAG.
    response: "...ok" then "HTTP/1.1 200 OK ... PCBFLAG_5c0cdaf0a128e2b7b7f57f663a2df8a8"

passed                          : true  (validate_case, Variant A)

--- data-quality / negative controls (--with-v2) ---
_seed_on_v2  (original blocked on V2) : 400 Bad Request, no flag  -> original_blocked_on_v2=true
    (whitespace-before-colon rejection from CVE-2019-16869 still present in 4.1.44)
_residual_on_v2 (residual blocked V2) : 400 Bad Request, no flag  -> residual_blocked_on_v2=true
    (CVE-2020-7238 fix throws "Both 'Content-Length: 5' and 'Transfer-Encoding: chunked' found")

VERDICT: GATE PASSED. Genuine same-sink incomplete-fix pair; single-server
differentiable (Netty is the origin server deciding accept/reject of the malformed
framing, observed directly via the pipelined smuggled request — not a downstream
forwarding/normalization difference).

Teardown: PCB_FLAG=teardown docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down
-v --rmi all  +  docker image prune -f. All three netty-cve-2020-7238-v{0,1,2} images
removed; maven/temurin base kept. Scratch diffs cleaned.
